# Formatting Rules (Biome/Ultracite)

## Core Settings

| Setting | Value |
|---------|-------|
| Quotes | Double `"` |
| Semicolons | Always |
| Indentation | Tabs (width: 2) |
| Line width | 80 characters |
| Trailing commas | All |
| JSX quotes | Double |

## Do

```typescript
// ✅ Double quotes
const name = "Jesse";

// ✅ Semicolons
const value = 42;

// ✅ Trailing commas
const obj = {
  first: 1,
  second: 2,
};

// ✅ Arrow functions for callbacks
items.map((item) => item.value);

// ✅ Template literals
const greeting = `Hello, ${name}!`;
```

## Don't

```typescript
// ❌ Single quotes
const name = 'Jesse';

// ❌ Missing semicolons
const value = 42

// ❌ No trailing commas
const obj = {
  first: 1,
  second: 2
};
```

## Import Organization

```typescript
// ✅ Correct order: external → internal → relative
import { NextResponse } from "next/server";
import { useState } from "react";

import { db } from "@/lib/db";
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";

import { localHelper } from "./helpers";
import type { LocalType } from "./types";
```

## Biome Ignore Comments

```typescript
// When you must disable a rule:
// biome-ignore lint/category/ruleName: explanation why

// Example:
// biome-ignore lint/security/noDangerouslySetInnerHtml: content is sanitized
<div dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: sanitizedHtml }} />
```

## Commands

```bash
pnpm check    # Check for issues
pnpm fix      # Auto-fix issues
```
